language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Futoshiki: fill an N by N grid with the digits 1 to N so that every row and column contains each digit once and the given inequalities hold.
$ grid size N, taken from the instance values
given values_dim1 : int
$ given digits of the puzzle, 0 for an empty cell
given values : matrix indexed by [int(1..values_dim1), int(1..values_dim1)] of int
$ number of inequality clues, taken from the instance lt list
given lt_dim1 : int
$ each clue lt[k,..] = (r1, c1, r2, c2) says cell (r1,c1) is less than cell (r2,c2), 1-based
given lt : matrix indexed by [int(1..lt_dim1), int(1..4)] of int
$ the completed grid
find grid : matrix indexed by [int(1..values_dim1), int(1..values_dim1)] of int(1..values_dim1)
such that
$ the digits that are given in the puzzle are kept in their cells
forAll r : int(1..values_dim1) . forAll c : int(1..values_dim1) . ((values[r,c] != 0) -> (grid[r,c] = values[r,c])),
$ each row contains each digit once
forAll r : int(1..values_dim1) . allDiff(grid[r,..]),
$ each column contains each digit once
forAll c : int(1..values_dim1) . allDiff(grid[..,c]),
$ each inequality clue must be honoured: the first cell is lower than the second cell
forAll k : int(1..lt_dim1) . (grid[lt[k,1], lt[k,2]] < grid[lt[k,3], lt[k,4]])
